{{Quote|Mandalorian vambraces? Where did you get these?''"<br />"''Try them on. Grappling line, paralyzing darts, repulsor. All designed to combat the abilities of the Jedi.|Sabine Wren and Fenn Rau|<ref name="Trials of the Darksaber" />}}
'''Mandalorian vambraces''' were forearm brace-like devices designed to combat the [[Force power|Force abilities]] of a [[Jedi]], but were also utilized for many other combative purposes. Vambraces could be equipped with a large array of different [[weapon]]s, such as [[blaster]]s, [[dart]]s, [[flamethrower]]s, [[Missile|rockets]], [[vibroblade]]s, and [[Whipcord launcher|whipcords]]. The [[Mandalorian]]s developed these vambraces alongside [[Mandalorian armor|their]] [[armor]] as a reaction to the Jedi's abilities encountered during the [[Mandalorian-Jedi War]].

==Description==
===Overview===
[[Mandalorian]] [[vambrace]]s were combat gear designed to counteract the [[Force power|Force abilities]] of a [[Jedi]].<ref name="Mandalorian Vambraces">{{Databank|mandalorian-vambraces|Mandalorian Vambraces}}</ref> As such, they were equipped with various [[weapon]]s that also proved useful against other foes. What was specifically on each pair of vambraces varied depending on the owner's fighting style. Like [[Mandalorian armor|their]] [[armor]], a Mandalorian's vambraces were made of [[beskar]], making them impervious to [[lightsaber]] attacks. A few Mandalorians had touchscreen displays on their vambraces, allowing them to control systems and weapons.<ref name="Legacy of Mandalore" />

===Individual variations===
====Jango and Boba Fett's vambraces====
[[File:BobaFett-BHUSC.png|thumb|left|250px|Boba Fett's vambraces]]
[[Jango Fett|Jango]] and [[Boba Fett]]'s vambraces were equipped with a variety of different offensive and defensive capabilities. His right vambrace had a [[Targeting laser|laser targeting system]]. Beneath that, was a tiny launcher for [[Homing beacon|tracking devices]]. Right below that was a [[dart]] launcher, capable of firing [[Tranquilizer dart|tranquilizer]], stun, shock, or explosive darts. On the other side of his right vambrace, was a [[whipcord launcher]], which could fire a 25-meter-long [[fibercord whip]]. On his left vambrace, was a [[Micro-Rocket Armor-Mounting]]; which could accommodate a wide variety of [[Wrist rocket|micro-rockets]], including [[MM9 mini concussion rocket launcher|MM9 concussion]] [[missile]]s from [[Kelvarek Consolidated Arms]].<ref name="Boba Bio Gallery">{{Databank|boba-fett-biography-gallery|Boba Fett Biography Gallery}}</ref>

Off to the side was a [[ZX miniature flame projector]] from [[Czerka Arms]], that when combined with a reinforced fuel line connected to his [[Z-6 jetpack]], could provide a steady supply of fuel for up to three minutes. Further down on the left vambrace, was a [[holoprojector]], communications system, and a [[Dur-24 wrist laser]] from [[BlasTech Industries]].<ref name="Boba Bio Gallery" /> However, while his vambraces contained multi-purpose buttons and switches, they did not contain a touchscreen display. Fett also integrated a [[chain code]] into his armor's vambraces.<ref name="Chapter 14">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 14: The Tragedy}}</ref>

====Bo-Katan Kryze's vambraces====
[[File:KryzeApprehendsAlmec-OFNF.png|thumb|right|250px|Bo-Katan Kryze uses one of her vambraces]]
The [[Nite Owls|Nite Owl]] [[Bo-Katan Kryze]] utilized vambraces since her time as a member of [[Death Watch]] during the [[Clone Wars]], and later during the [[Imperial Era|Imperial]] and [[New Republic Era]]s. Her left vambrace contained a [[Personal Combat Shield|shield projector]].<ref name="Old Friends Not Forgotten">{{TCW|Old Friends Not Forgotten}}</ref> The right vambrace was equipped with a [[wrist blaster]],<ref name="A Friend in Need">{{TCW|A Friend in Need}}</ref> [[electroshock dart]]s,<ref name="Chapter 22">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 22: Guns for Hire}}</ref> a [[Vibroblade|wrist vibroblade]],<ref name="Chapter 11">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 11: The Heiress}}</ref> and a whipcord launcher.<ref name="Chapter 18">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 18: The Mines of Mandalore}}</ref>

====Din Djarin's vambraces====
[[File:DjarinVambraces-SWGG.png|thumb|left|250px|Din Djarin's vambraces]]
[[Din Djarin]] owned vambraces that were forged by [[the Armorer]]. The vambraces supplemented Djarin's other weapons and fighting techniques. As such, many features were substituted for a more complementary style. His left vambrace was equipped with [[whistling bird]]s, allowing him to launch twelve miniature explosive projectiles at once.<ref name="Chapter 3" /> Djarin had a whipcord launcher in both of his vambraces, allowing him to fire slightly less durable but significantly longer lariats. Both vambraces were also equipped with a [[flamethrower]] as well as a fuel tank, enabling him to operate without the need of his jetpack. Djarin could control his jetpack with his right vambrace, even if it was not on him.<ref name="Chapter 1">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 1: The Mandalorian}}</ref><ref name="Chapter 10">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 10: The Passenger}}</ref>

====Sabine Wren's vambraces====
[[File:Personal_Combat_Shield_SWL.png|thumb|right|250px|Sabine Wren's vambraces]]
[[Sabine Wren]]'s vambraces were a gift from [[Protector of Concord Dawn]], [[Fenn Rau]].<ref name="Trials of the Darksaber" /> They were similar to Fett's, yet the left vambrace contained a shield projector above the laser targeting system and motion detectors below the [[paralyzing dart]]s and [[Repulsorlift|repulsor]]. The right vambrace was equipped with an electroshock device,<ref name="Crawler Commandeers">{{Rebels|Crawler Commandeers}}</ref> a flamethrower, and a [[grappling line]]. Both of Wren's vambraces contained touchscreen displays, providing her with an alternate means of monitoring and controlling weapons, [[sensor]]s, communications systems, and the [[heads-up display]] inside her helmet.<ref name="Legacy of Mandalore" />

==History==
[[File:Jango_wrist_blades.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Jango Fett's vambraces]]
Following the Mandalorians' [[Mandalorian-Jedi War|war]] against the Jedi, they developed vambraces to work in tandem with their armor to combat the Jedi's abilities.<ref name="Star Wars Rebels Showrunner Explains Major Knight of the Old Republic Reference">{{WebCite|url=http://comicbook.com/starwars/2017/02/18/star-wars-rebels-knights-of-the-old-republic-reference-confirmed|text=Star Wars Rebels Showrunner Explains Major Knight of the Old Republic Reference|author=Lucas Siegel|archivedate=20170220002112}}</ref> [[Bounty hunter]]s, such as the famed Mandalorian mercenary and [[foundling]]<ref name="SWCEUAE">''[[Star Wars: Character Encyclopedia, Updated and Expanded Edition]]''</ref> [[Jango Fett]],<ref name="AoR - JF">[[Age of Republic - Jango Fett 1|''Age of Republic - Jango Fett'' 1]]</ref> and later<ref name="The Empire Strikes Back">{{Film|V}}</ref> his son Boba, used them in their line of work.<ref name="Attack of the Clones">{{Film|II}}</ref>

Death Watch leader [[Pre Vizsla]]<ref name="Shades of Reason" /> and his followers, such as Bo-Katan Kryze, used vambraces during Death Watch's [[Exile (punishment)|exile]] from [[Mandalore]]. Vizsla used vambraces when he [[Battle on Carlac|fought]] Jedi [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]],<ref name="A Friend In Need" /> forces of the [[Hutt Clan]],<ref name="Eminence">{{TCW|Eminence (episode)}}</ref> and when he dueled the renegade [[Sith Lord]] [[Maul]] for control of the [[Shadow Collective]].<ref name="Shades of Reason" />

[[File:Sabine_Mando_vambraces.png|thumb|right|300px|Sabine Wren holds up Mandalorian vambraces]]
During her training with the [[Darksaber]] in [[2 BBY]], Sabine Wren used her vambraces in combat with [[Jedi Knight]] [[Kanan Jarrus]] and his Padawan [[Ezra Bridger]]. After learning to fight with the vambraces and Darksaber combined, she was able to defeat both Force users.<ref name="Trials of the Darksaber" /> The post-[[Great Purge of Mandalore|Great Purge]] Mandalorian group known as [[the Tribe]] also used vambraces.<ref name="Chapter 1" /> In [[9 ABY]], the Mandalorian bounty hunter Din Djarin utilized vambraces in battling [[Moff]] [[Gideon]]'s [[Gideon's Imperial remnant|Imperial remnant]] on multiple occasions.<ref name="Chapter 3">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 3: The Sin}}</ref><ref name="Chapter 16">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 16: The Rescue}}</ref><ref name="Chapter 23">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 23: The Spies}}</ref>

In [[35 ABY]],<ref name="Date-35">{{FilmDate|IX|Diss's appearance}}</ref> the bounty hunter [[Carib Diss]] wore a Mandalorian vambrace equipped with whistling birds while residing on [[Kijimi]].<ref name="TROS VD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Mandalorians are prideful, brilliant warriors in their own right. They're also technologically savvy and advanced. This is how they've fought the Jedi. So again this kind of plays into the opening with Tarre Vizsla in the images of them fighting. So you're seeing here almost a small re-enactment of a Jedi-Mandalorian war and how a Mandalorian would get the upper hand, surprising Jedi with technology and then cutting them down, finishing them off. So they'd get this advantage.|Dave Filoni|<ref name="Complete Season Three">[[Star Wars Rebels: Complete Season Three|''Star Wars Rebels'': Complete Season Three]]</ref>}}
The Mandalorian vambrace first appeared with Boba Fett in [[Star Wars: Episode V The Empire Strikes Back|''Star Wars'': Episode V ''The Empire Strikes Back'']].<ref name="The Empire Strikes Back" /> They were first identified as such in the animated TV series ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]''{{'}} [[Star Wars Rebels Season Three|season three]] episode ''[[Trials of the Darksaber]]''.<ref name="Trials of the Darksaber" />

